
================================================
 mouse-joystick-pcb  stage 5: analog angle output
================================================
 Requires 36 V and a v0.3 or later board.
 The motor is not touched. Send 'b' to begin.

commands
  ?  this menu
  b  rail up, bus closed, DAC configured
  z  output zero scale (code 0)
  m  output midscale
  f  output full scale (code 0xFFFF)
  v  set an output voltage, digits then Enter (mV)
  c  set a raw code, digits then Enter
  s  the three-point fit: 0, midscale, full scale, with a
     pause at each for a meter reading
  t  step 0 -> full scale, for the filter group delay
  q  what the driver knows: gain, full scale, LSB
  d  DEVID and STATUS -- I2C builds only, see below
  r  soft reset the DAC (blocks data writes until 'b')
  x  power down: bus open, HV_EN low
  B  reboot into BOOTSEL      R  reboot

Every value printed is COMMANDED, never measured. This
board cannot read its own analog output, and over SPI it
cannot read the DAC's registers either. Use a DMM.


##### send 'b' at +5.0 s
[1] rail
    [ ok ] +3.3V_SW up in 132 ms
[2] bus switch
    [ ok ] closed. GP10/GP11/GP13 now reach the DAC.
[3] SPI1
    [ ok ] SCK GP10, TX GP11, SYNC GP13
[4] DAC configuration
    [ ok ] GAIN 0x101, full scale 2.5000 V at the DAC, 3.3000 V at the BNC
    [note] NOT VERIFIED, and cannot be: this transport
      is SPI and the DAC80501 has no SDO pin. The only
      check on GAIN is measuring the output against the
      expected full scale above. Strapping SPI2C for I2C
      would make this a real read -- see the pcb plan.


##### send 'q' at +8.3 s
  configured:   yes
  GAIN written: 0x101
  REF-DIV 1, BUFF-GAIN 1
  DAC full scale: 2.500000 V
  BNC full scale: 3.300000 V
  one LSB:        38.15 uV at the DAC, 50.35 uV at the BNC
  last code:      0


##### send 'm' at +10.4 s
    code 32768 (0x8000)  -> DAC 1.250000 V  -> BNC 1.650000 V expected

##### send 'f' at +12.5 s
    code 65535 (0xFFFF)  -> DAC 2.499962 V  -> BNC 3.299950 V expected

##### send 't' at +14.6 s
Step 0 -> full scale on FW_TRIG1's rising edge, then back
after 100 ms. Scope the BNC against InstrumentPort TRIG1
(J1501 pin 28) and read the delay to 50% of the step.
Expect about 266 us of group delay from the 2-pole 987 Hz
Sallen-Key, and roughly 2 ms to settle to one OneBox LSB.
That delay is the FILTER, not firmware latency.
  stepped.


##### send 'z' at +16.8 s
    code 0 (0x0)  -> DAC 0.000000 V  -> BNC 0.000000 V expected

##### send 'x' at +18.9 s
Powered down: DAC at zero scale, bus open, HV_EN low.
+36V_SW takes about 700 ms to bleed down.
The DAC lost VDD, so its GAIN is back to a 5.0 V full
scale. Data writes are blocked again until 'b'.

